# Re-measure receipts for ROLLING from-url rows.
#
# Format: <dest>  sha256=<64-hex>  measured=<YYYY-MM-DD>  result=pass
#         remeasure=<script>[:<arg>...]  evidence=<repo-relative path>
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A rolling row's digest fails closed when upstream
# rebuilds the asset, and the cheapest way to make a red tree green is to paste
# the new digest into `from-url`. That one-line diff looks like housekeeping and
# is actually a verifier swap: every claim the old verifier established is now
# resting on a verifier nobody ran. So the pin is not enough on its own -- a
# rolling digest must ALSO name the run that judged those exact bytes.
#
# `lint-verifier-jar-provenance.ts` refuses a rolling pin with no row here whose
# sha256 matches, whose result is `pass`, whose `remeasure=` is the one the
# manifest row declares (a weaker command does not buy the pin), and whose
# evidence file exists. `bun tools/setup/repin-rolling.ts <dest>` writes the row
# only after running that command itself and seeing it exit 0.
#
# THE HONEST LIMIT, stated so nobody mistakes this for a proof: a hand-written
# row passes. Nothing here can distinguish an earned receipt from a typed one --
# the same admission the AgencySignature block makes about copied attestations.
# What the file buys is that the laundering is no longer a ONE-LINE diff that
# reads as maintenance; it is a second, explicit, reviewable assertion about a
# run that either happened or did not.
#
# Rows are APPEND-ONLY and historical rows stay. The digest that is live is
# whichever one `from-url` currently pins; the rest are the lineage.
#
